# GitHub public quality (tvscreener-rs)

Treat every README as if it could be public tomorrow.

## Product voice

- **tvscreener-rs** is an unofficial Rust TradingView Screener HTTP client (+ optional MCP).
- **Not affiliated with TradingView.** Keep that clear; do not invent affiliation.

## Sensitive / internal (keep out of README, docs, Makefile, scripts)

Do **not** put these in committed product text:

- Host-absolute paths (any `/…` machine layout)
- Screen recipes, agent handoff tone
- "Worker fork" / Cursor agent merge cuisine as the main contributor story
- Cursor plan/stage IDs
- Shared credential file paths

## Plan jargon allowlist

**Forbidden** in: code, comments, commit subjects/bodies, PR titles/bodies, README, public docs, MCP tool names/descriptions.

**Allowed only** in:

- `.cursor/plans/*`

## Conventional commits and PRs

Subject (≤72 chars):

```text
<type>(optional-scope): summary in imperative
```

Types: `feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `refactor` | `test` | `chore` | `ci`.

PR title = same grammar. Body: Summary + Test plan only. Do **not** append "Made with Cursor".

## Signing and merge checklist (every PR)

1. Author Interchouette; every local commit SSH-signed (`commit.gpgsign=true`).
2. On the **fork**: `git fetch interchouette && git rebase interchouette/dev`, resolve, push to `interchouette` (signed).
3. PR up to date with org `dev`; always `--reviewer gRoussac`.
4. Confirm PR head Verified.
5. Wait for **gRoussac** Approve (org `dev` requires **1** approving review + code owner), then `gh pr merge --squash` (never `gh pr merge --rebase` onto org). Never merge when `reviews` lacks `APPROVED` from **gRoussac**.
6. Sync fork `dev` from `upstream/dev`.

See `github-fork-pr.mdc`.
